GENESIS I

1.

In the [Beginning | בְּרֵאשִׁית | Bereshit | /bə.reːˈʃiːt/], [God | אֱלֹהִים | Elohim | /ʔeloˈhim/] created the [Heavens | שָׁמַיִם | Shamayim | /ʃa.maˈjim/] and the [Earth | אֶרֶץ | Eretz | /ˈʔɛ.rɛt͡s/].

In the beginning God created the heavens and the earth.

2.

The [Earth | אֶרֶץ | Eretz | /ˈʔɛ.rɛt͡s/] was formless and empty. Darkness was upon the face of the [Deep | תְּהוֹם | Tehom | /təˈhom/], and the [Spirit | רוּחַ | Ruach | /ˈru.aχ/] of [God | אֱלֹהִים | Elohim | /ʔeloˈhim/] hovered over the face of the [Waters | מַיִם | Mayim | /ˈma.jim/].

The earth was waste and empty; and darkness was on the surface of the deep. God’s Spirit was hovering over the surface of the waters.

3.

Then [God | אֱלֹהִים | Elohim | /ʔeloˈhim/] said, “Let there be [Light | אוֹר | Or | /ʔoːr/],” and there was [Light | אוֹר | Or | /ʔoːr/].

God said, “Let there be light,” and there was light.

4.

[God | אֱלֹהִים | Elohim | /ʔeloˈhim/] saw the [Light | אוֹר | Or | /ʔoːr/], that it was good; and [God | אֱלֹהִים | Elohim | /ʔeloˈhim/] divided the [Light | אוֹר | Or | /ʔoːr/] from the [Darkness | חֹשֶׁךְ | Choshekh | /ˈχo.ʃɛχ/].

God saw the light, and saw that it was good. God divided the light from the darkness.

5.

[God | אֱלֹהִים | Elohim | /ʔeloˈhim/] called the [Light | אוֹר | Or | /ʔoːr/] Day, and the [Darkness | חֹשֶׁךְ | Choshekh | /ˈχo.ʃɛχ/] he called Night. There was evening and there was morning, the first day.

God called the light Day, and the darkness he called Night. There was evening and there was morning, the first day.